WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.400
Container image security depends on the supply chain as well as runtime settings.

2
00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:08.373
A production image can include base layers, .

3
00:00:08.373 --> 00:00:19.251
NET runtime components, NuGet packages, native libraries, operating system packages, build tools used earlier in the pipeline, CI actions, and application code.

4
00:00:19.251 --> 00:00:23.633
Each layer and dependency has ownership and update implications.

5
00:00:23.633 --> 00:00:28.407
Image scanning should be part of the pipeline, but findings need triage.

6
00:00:28.407 --> 00:00:37.407
Teams should review severity, affected layer, reachable component, deployment exposure, available fix, and compensating controls.

7
00:00:37.407 --> 00:00:47.032
The goal is not to ignore findings or accept every result blindly; it is to create a response process that is fast, evidence-based, and repeatable.

8
00:00:47.032 --> 00:00:50.475
SBOMs help teams understand what is inside an image.

9
00:00:50.475 --> 00:00:58.145
They support vulnerability response, customer requests, incident review, license review, and rebuild planning.

10
00:00:58.145 --> 00:01:07.535
An SBOM is most useful when it is generated consistently, stored with the image or release, and connected to the team that owns the application.

11
00:01:07.535 --> 00:01:13.170
Old images can contain old base layers even when the application code has not changed.

12
00:01:13.170 --> 00:01:20.839
Regular rebuilds are important because a rebuild can pick up patched base image layers and refreshed dependencies.

13
00:01:20.839 --> 00:01:29.134
Pinning versions improves repeatability, but it must be paired with an update workflow so pins do not become permanent drift.

14
00:01:29.134 --> 00:01:38.994
Trusted registries, image signatures, provenance metadata, least-privilege registry access, and cleanup of stale images should all be reviewed.

15
00:01:38.994 --> 00:01:41.342
The registry is part of production.

16
00:01:41.342 --> 00:01:51.437
Teams should know who can publish images, who can pull them, how tags are promoted, how rollbacks work, and how retired images are removed from active use.
